    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "# Diagram Your Card\r\n\r\nYou are designing the layout for a single card. You need to decide which data fields belong in which part of the card.\r\n\r\n## Steps\r\n1. **Review the Schema:** Look at the \"Data Schema\" panel and review the data types for each field (e.g., `string`, `number`, `boolean`).\r\n2. **Map Fields to Layout:** Drag and drop items from the \"Card Elements\" panel into the \"Card View\" panel. Then draw a line from each schema field to the corresponding section on the \"Card Layout\" (Title, Image, etc.).\r\n3. **Indicate Fallback Options:** Notice that `rating`, `imageURL`, and `summary` can be `null`. Add a note with fallback options for each field. For example, what should show if the image is missing?"
  },
